From: hal@alumni.cco.caltech.edu (Hal Finney)
Subject: EXT/LONGEVITY: Identity life-span.

The current issue of Extropy has an interview with Mark Miller in which
he discusses his "credit" theory of identity.  The idea is that we may
be so different in the far future that  we would have less in common with
our present selves than, say, we have today in common with snails.  On
what basis can we say that we are the same person?  Miller argues that
whomever the future self gives "credit" as being its younger self should
be considered to be the earlier identity of that person.  Miller's "credit"
includes such concepts as respect, admiration, and influence.

In this sense, many of our list members may look back, millenia from now,
and see themselves as expanded versions of Ayn Rand, not of some little
computer programmer pounding away in a cubicle somewhere.  (Half :-).

Hal

